# NIST CAVP response files (RFC-006): vendored VERBATIM, byte-identical
# to the upstream zip contents, with provenance sha256 hashes recorded in
# docs/rfc-006-sha512.handoff.md. They are native CRLF; without this
# entry, a checkout-side core.autocrlf=input setting normalizes CRLF to
# LF on `git add` (verified empirically while vendoring these files),
# silently invalidating the recorded hashes for every future clone. `-text`
# disables all newline conversion so the stored blob and every checkout
# stay byte-exact.
tests/vectors/*.rsp -text
